  "sourceScope": "An original concise account of the central method from official author excerpts, not a complete EPUB. Selected explanations and cases were read in chapters 1 (second edition), 2–3, 9–10 and 14, supplemented by Rosenberg’s own explanations and a CNVC cross-check. The chapter-2 sample explicitly identifies the third edition, ©2019; chapter 14 is an NVC3 excerpt. This is not a summary of every chapter or a collation of one printing. Source notes identify the reading boundaries. RU and EN are new accounts, not an official translation. The author’s model is not presented as proof of therapeutic efficacy. Primary coverage includes the author’s process and Felix illustration; demands/blame definition; observation and the principal/Phil cases; mourning/self-forgiveness and the suit; anger, John, reflection and reminder card; and appreciation’s three components and participant case. The main-book protective-force chapter was not directly read: only the principle in official author quotes is retained and cross-checked with CNVC, whose later explanation is attributed to Myra Walden. Exact source roles, consulted sections, edition distinctions and all screen evidence locators are in sources.md. No full owned edition was found by the scoped Apple Books title/package-metadata search; no purchase, loan, credential request, unofficial full-book search or access bypass occurred.",
